FULIST                                                    (VM/370plus) CMS EXEC
Use the FULIST command to work with CMS files from a full-screen list of them,
in the manner of IBM's FILELIST.  FL is a short form.
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
| FULIST   | [fn|* [ft|* [fm|A|*]]]                                           |
| FL       |                                                                  |
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
fn, ft   file name and type; * or a prefix followed by * selects several.
fm       the file mode; the default is A, * means all accessed disks.

The list shows Cmd, Filename, Filetype, Fm, Format, Lrecl, Records, Blocks,
Date and Time (and the disk label on a 132-column screen).

Commands in the Cmd column
Type a command next to one or more files and press ENTER.  The commands run
from the top of the screen down.  In a command:
   /    stands for the whole file id "fn ft fm"
   /n   the file name,  /t  the file type,  /m  the file mode
A command without a / gets " /" appended.  Abbreviations:
   E or X    edit the file (EE)
   B         browse the file (FSVIEW)
   D         discard (erase) the file
   =         repeat the last command
Any other CMS or CP command may be used, e.g.  COPYFILE / = = B  or
RENAME / NEW = =  or  PRINT /.  After a command the column shows  *  if it
ended with return code 0, otherwise  *rc.

PF keys
   PF1  Help             PF7   Backward (a page)
   PF2  Refresh          PF8   Forward  (a page)
   PF3  Quit             PF9   FL /n: all files with this file name
   PF4  Sort by type     PF10  Sort by name
   PF5  Sort by date     PF11  Edit the file under the cursor
   PF6  Sort by size     PF12  Cursor: list <-> command line

The command line (====>)
   TOP, BOTTOM           go to the top or the end of the list
   SORT NAME|TYPE|DATE|SIZE
   REFRESH               read the list again
   FULIST fn ft fm       list other files
   QUIT                  leave FULIST
   anything else         run as a CMS or CP command

FULIST uses the REXX full-screen package (HELP REXXEXT FULLSCRE) and needs a
3270 terminal.
